  "estimatedMinutes": null,
  "statement": "The polynomial \\(f(x)=x^{3}-3 x^{2}-4 x+4\\) has three real roots \\(r_{1}, r_{2}\\), and \\(r_{3}\\). Let \\(g(x)=\\) \\(x^{3}+a x^{2}+b x+c\\) be the polynomial which has roots \\(s_{1}, s_{2}\\), and \\(s_{3}\\), where \\(s_{1}=r_{1}+r_{2} z+r_{3} z^{2}\\), \\(s_{2}=r_{1} z+r_{2} z^{2}+r_{3}, s_{3}=r_{1} z^{2}+r_{2}+r_{3} z\\), and \\(z=\\frac{-1+i \\sqrt{3}}{2}\\). Find the real part of the sum of the coefficients of \\(g(x)\\).",
